    "description": "Member of agile team responsible for encryption system to deliver Comcast cable television services to customers.\n\nSecure Media Client Integration\n---------------------------------------------------------\nIntegrated the Comcast SecureMedia SteelKnot DRM client with the JavaScript/C++ browser using the OpenCDM interface.  Created a new facet of the message passing protocol, and became the team expert on the messaging architecture in the process.\n\nSecure Media License Server\n---------------------------------------------------------\nResponsible for creation of SDK for Comcast’s License Server validation.  Replaced cURL scripts used for client communication with a DRM Client Simulator during my spare time to simplify testing. Requested by management to continue maintenance on DRM Client Simulator, and presented the SDK integration with the Simulator to Comcast senior management.\n\nEntitlement Control Message Generator\n---------------------------------------------------------\nWorked on generator that sent Entitlement Control Messages (ECMs) to the client, and validated the responses.  The team had begun transitioning to the Scala development language before my arrival, and I quickly picked up Scala to keep pace.  Identified code inefficiencies and reduced execution time from 20 minutes to just a minute and a half.\n",
